{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784301839,"nonce":"DgxtXzKuA1J+eY93NedRlEZFisU=","title":"[dogfood] handoff runbook: App must subscribe to events + grant statuses:write, or the loop silently half-works","message":"Dogfooding surfaced two GitHub App-config gaps that the handoff's setup steps don't guard against, and both fail SILENTLY end-to-end:\n\n1. Event subscriptions: the App had events:[] (webhook URL+secret configured, but no 'Subscribe to events' boxes checked). Result: push/pull_request are NEVER delivered, so no runs trigger — yet installation/installation_repositories events STILL arrive (they're App-management events, independent of the subscription list), so the connection registers and /v1/repos looks healthy. Very confusing: 'repo is registered but nothing runs'. Had to drive runs via hand-signed synthetic deliveries.\n\n2. Permissions: the App was granted contents:read, metadata:read, packages:read, pull_requests:read, repository_hooks:read — but NOT statuses:write (nor checks:write). So commit-status posting 403s and (per the silent-swallow bug) leaves the loop looking green locally while the PR shows no status.\n\nRunbook improvements: (a) the setup doc should call out 'Subscribe to events: Push + Pull request' as REQUIRED and verifiable (App events list), and 'Commit statuses: write' as REQUIRED for status deep-links; (b) consider a /v1 preflight/doctor that mints an installation token and reports the granted permissions + subscribed events vs what Scarab needs, so misconfig is caught at setup, not by a dead-silent pipeline.\n\nApp id 4323648, installation 147197357, repo thulasi-ram/scarab-ci.","files":null}]}